## Hints for Future Agents
The post-commit hook automatically pushes master. Use git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit for local-only commits; do not change the repository-wide hook configuration. Metadata edits reject a flow-style top-level mapping or an edit that would invalidate an alias, preserving the original file. The failed-write regression runs a subprocess with RLIMIT_FSIZE so the parent test process is unaffected. Symlink resolution on macOS can change /var paths to /private/var, so both corpus paths and lookup paths need canonicalization. Golden tests copy the external-parent fixture as well as plans so relative parent validation still works. The unrelated Herdr configuration edit must remain outside this commit. A concurrent Makefile edit was committed separately as dad1582 before this commit.

## Codebase Discoveries
YAML unmarshalling can leave partially decoded fields on a plan whose metadata is invalid. The tree uses those parent fields, so cycle detection must follow them as well. Replacing absolute paths after rendering a table does not normalize the widths of headers or external-parent rows. JSON-encoded strings preserve line breaks and control characters when decoded as YAML.

